Diagnosed MSYS2 initialization failure and devised corrective setup solution

This is MSYS2's first-run initialization failure — after a fresh install, the login shell exits 1 until its /etc/profile setup completes. The script calls bash too soon.
Ran 2 commands, read a file

Root cause: Fresh MSYS2 installs require msys2_shell.cmd to run once to generate /etc/fstab, home directories, and profile scripts. Calling bash --login before that happens exits with code 1 every time.

What v3 fixes:

    Runs msys2_shell.cmd -defterm -no-start -mingw64 -c "exit 0" first to trigger initialization
    Follows with a bare bash --login -c "echo init" (exit code ignored) to let /etc/profile settle
    Adds $env:MSYSTEM = "MINGW64" and $env:CHERE_INVOKING = "1" before every subsequent bash call so the correct MinGW64 toolchain path loads reliably

Replace your .ps1 with the new one and run the same command:
powershell

.\Install-CTW11-Win11.ps1

If MSYS2 was already partially installed from the failed attempt, the script will detect it at C:\msys64 and skip reinstalling — it will proceed straight to the init fix.
