What was causing all three parser errors and how this version avoids them:

The && error, missing terminator, and missing } all came from the same root cause — passing multiline bash command strings inline inside PowerShell. PS 5.1 tries to parse && as its own operator and chokes on $PATH, backticks, and unclosed quotes inside those strings.

This version writes every bash command to a .sh file on disk first using [IO.File]::WriteAllText(), then calls bash --login "/home/script.sh". PowerShell never sees a single bash character — no parsing conflicts possible.

