Identified Android GNSS Logger format and diagnosed parser incompatibility

That's Android GNSS Logger format — completely different from NMEA. The parser needs to read Fix rows where column 2 is lat and column 3 is lon, with Provider field telling us GPS vs Network. Current parser was looking for $G... NMEA sentences — found nothing.
Ran 4 commands, viewed a file, read a file

Copy the new .c to C:\msys64\home\ctw11_build\ and rerun Fix-MSYS2-CTW11.ps1 to recompile.

What was wrong and what's fixed:

The file you showed is Android GNSS Logger format — a Google measurement app that logs everything the phone's sensors see. The old parser only knew NMEA $GPRMC/$GPGGA sentences, so it found zero coordinates.

The new parse_android_gnss_log() function:

    Reads the # Fix,Provider,... header line to find exactly which column number holds LatitudeDegrees, LongitudeDegrees, Provider, AltitudeMeters, UnixTimeMillis, NumberOfUsedSignals, etc. — so it's immune to column order changes between logger versions
    Falls back to positional columns Fix,provider(1),lat(2),lon(3) if the header comment is missing
    Provider field drives the dot shape — gps/gnss → orange circle, anything else (network, fused, passive) → blue diamond
    MockLocation=1 is flagged as network/cell automatically
    Raw records (pseudorange measurements) get attached to the most recent Fix coordinate for the detail popup
    is_android_gnss_log() sniff-detects the format by scanning the first 20 lines for UncalAccel, ConstellationType, Fix,Provider, etc. — so you don't have to rename files

